  "id": "dyslogia",
  "term": "dyslogia",
  "definition": "Dyslogia is a historical term suggested as an alternative name for alogia: an inability to speak that is attributed to an intellectual or thought-formation disorder rather than to aphasia. In this usage, speech is not acquired or becomes impossible because of a mental difficulty.",
